keywords:
  - graph neural networks
  - adaptive message passing
  - cross-spectral analysis
  - nominal-relative control
  - model predictive control
  - risk-aware deployment
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Post-training transport control for frozen graph neural networks: a common adapter at the native aggregation call,
  a registered ten-action transport family, label-free cross-spectral and confidence measurements, a conditioned
  observer with one-step and sequence risk models, nine policy families compared against the strongest cross-fitted
  open-loop comparator, held-out mechanism confirmation and statistically regimed admission with exact comparator
  fallback. Seven-dataset implementation (ogbn-arxiv, ogbn-proteins, ogbn-products, Roman-empire, PascalVOC-SP,
  COCO-SP, Peptides-func) with a sealed eight-stage lifecycle, numerical replay, checkpoint re-execution and a
  machine-readable registry of the manuscript's constants and reported results.
